PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key requirements: (1) sole directors = Alex + Tyler for equal ops control + 50/50 voting shares; (2) Tyler needs dividend-eligible shares; (3) Alex needs only salary eligibility (possible for any director/officer, so his shares can be non-dividend); (4) authorized non-voting class usable for future investors (no operational say). 

Colleagues split sharply: A favored by 1/2/8/9/13 (identical A/B voting+div classes, holding co for Alex, useless Class C); B by 1/5/14/17 (wrong dividend assignment to Alex); C by 3/4/6/15/16/18 (correctly assigns non-div voting A to Alex + div voting B to Tyler, only two directors, non-voting C exists); E by 11 (usable non-voting dividend Class C but extra directors = sons break equal control); D by 7 (no non-voting class authorized); 12 says none works. 

Strongest pattern: C is only option that simultaneously satisfies differentiated dividend rights, two-director board, and non-voting investor class. Persistent issues: whether non-voting class must carry economic rights (question silent); possible drafting anomalies in C. No consensus yet; need to test each option against all four criteria in next round.}

